      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_unified_post_capture_sizing.py` aborts with exit -6 (`CUDBG_EXCEPTION_WARP_MMU_FAULT` in `_zero_pages_kernel`) since #42930. It was seen on the 5090 runner and reproduces on H200 (SM90); the parent of 8d229d96e0 passes.\n\nWith post-capture KV sizing, `UnifiedKVPool.finalize_backing` backs only the final byte prefix of the reserved VA, but the unified SWA allocator keeps pricing the whole reservation until `resize()` runs. An allocation in that window gets a top-end SWA page past the backed bytes (page 131071 of a 64 MiB reservation with 16 MiB backed). Before #42930 this only touched bookkeeping for MHA pools. #42930 zeroes MHA page envelopes on hand-out, so the same allocation now writes to unmapped memory.\n\nThe production path (`kv_pool_runtime.py`) calls `finalize_backing` and then `resize` straight away, so this was hit only by the test. It is still a latent fault for any allocation before `resize`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `UnifiedSWAAllocatorBase.__init__` sets `_awaiting_resize` when post-capture backing is active; `UnifiedSWATokenToKVPoolAllocator.resize()` clears it. `ensure_capacity()` raises until then; every allocation path goes through it.\n- Test: add \"allocation before finalize_backing\" (the construction-to-finalize window, where graph capture and prewarm run) and \"allocation between finalize_backing and resize\" subtests that expect the new error. The \"resize with live allocations\" subtest now allocates after `resize` and checks that a second `resize` is rejected as non-empty.\n\n## Test plan (H200)\n\n- `test_unified_post_capture_sizing.py`: OK (was 2 errors / MMU fault on HEAD)\n- `test_multi_ended_allocator`, `test_kv_index_translator`, `test_kv_cache_configurator_draft_gate`, `test_unified_handout_zeroing`, `test_fused_draft_placement`: OK\n\n### End-to-end (H200)\n\n`openai/gpt-oss-20b` (hybrid SWA, fa3) with the cookbook flags (`--reasoning-parser gpt-oss --tool-call-parser gpt-oss`, TP1) plus `--enable-unified-memory`. sgl-eval 0.1.3 gsm8k, 200 examples, temperature 1.0, top_p 1.0, reasoning effort low, max_tokens 8192.\n\n| Run | Startup path | gsm8k | Errors |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SGLANG_ENABLE_POST_CAPTURE_KV_SIZING=1` | Reserved VA, graph capture, then `finalize_backing` and `resize` (105 GB of KV) | 96.0% | 0 |\n| Baseline (post-capture off) | Pool allocated up front | 95.5% | 0 |\n\nThe post-capture server started cleanly with no \"cannot allocate before resize\" error, so nothing on the real startup path allocates before `resize`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38909380188](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38909380188)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38909379753](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38909379753)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38909380169](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38909380169)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
